From: bootani <bootani@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] kmsdrm: use XRGB8888 for the scanout surface

SDL creates its GBM scanout surface as ARGB8888. Some KMS drivers
(virtio-gpu, and primary planes on several others) only scan out
XRGB8888, so drmModeSetCrtc fails with EINVAL and SDL reports
"Could not set videomode on CRTC". The primary plane ignores alpha
anyway, so ask for XRGB8888, which every driver accepts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [bootani-specific]
---
--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-10-08 01:04:16.707042067 +0000
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-10-08 01:04:16.711856344 +0000
@@ -1193,7 +1193,7 @@
     SDL_VideoDisplay *display = SDL_GetDisplayForWindow(window);
     SDL_DisplayData *dispdata = (SDL_DisplayData *)display->driverdata;
 
-    uint32_t surface_fmt = GBM_FORMAT_ARGB8888;
+    uint32_t surface_fmt = GBM_FORMAT_XRGB8888;
     uint32_t surface_flags = GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT | GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING;
 
     EGLContext egl_context;
